    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "ugt5boiok8cx",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Rich Historical Tapestry of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "5txbo8wbzemn",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "2gnrhfvsip92"
              ],
              "text": "Qena"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "2gnrhfvsip92",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58902",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000003",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Qena, a town steeped in a blend of ancient and Islamic heritage, holds a significant place in Egypt’s historical narrative. Here’s an exploration of its storied past:"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ancient Beginnings and Greek Influence"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Originally named Caene (New Town) by the ancient Greeks, distinguishing it from the nearby "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000006"
              ],
              "text": "Coptos"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " (now Qifṭ)."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Located 23 km north of Coptos, it gradually took over the latter’s significant trade with Arabia, India, and China."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-copts-of-egypt-guardians-of-an-ancient-faith/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/ejiputo-no-koputo-kyoto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Trade and Route Changes"
            },
            {
              "_key": "lws0zgzxblsy",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The shift in trade prominence was due to a new northern route across the Eastern Desert to the ports of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "tfhj43pjs4cj",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "tqkvj5g0vbge"
              ],
              "text": "Safaga"
            },
            {
              "_key": "056gx78kyruq",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " and Al-Quṣier."
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Post-Mamlūk period (after 1517) archaeological findings at Al-Quṣier suggest the change in trade routes."
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Although trade diminished in the Ottoman period, this northern route persisted, especially for Upper Egyptians embarking on the hajj pilgrimage to Mecca."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "tqkvj5g0vbge",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58920",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000015",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Islamic Influence and Religious Significance"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Qena is not just an ancient trade hub but also a center of Islamic heritage."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Maghrebi Abd el-Rahim, upon returning from Mecca, established a Sufi center in Qena."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "His death in 1195 led to the construction of a mosque over his tomb, turning it into a pilgrimage site."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The large modern mosque of Sheikh el-Qenawi in the town’s main square highlights his enduring influence."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Modern Developments and Infrastructure"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The town experienced a revival during and after World War II."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Its strategic location as a terminus for the road to the Red Sea coast and its status as a governorate capital spurred growth."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The construction of a bridge across the Nile and the upgrading of the Upper "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001a"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " highway, passing through Qena, enhanced its importance."
            },
            {
              "_key": "idwubaxyldnw",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Qena is well-connected, served by the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "suohlwymbs3v",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "nybsthobojiv"
              ],
              "text": "Cairo"
            },
            {
              "_key": "o5d1lha3hfr6",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "–"
            },
            {
              "_key": "xwev0ztip5hk",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "4xfy91ojtxf3"
              ],
              "text": "Aswan"
            },
            {
              "_key": "p8xnyl2hybro",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " railway and a nearby military air base."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/faux-pas-to-avoid-in-egypt/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/ejiputo-de-shitsurei-ni-nara-nai-tame-ni",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "nybsthobojiv",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            },
            {
              "_key": "4xfy91ojtxf3",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Economic and Cultural Hub"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Today, Qena is a bustling market town and a service center for road vehicles."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Traditionally noted for producing porous clay water vessels, a craft that continues to this day."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "number",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Qena’s rich tapestry of history, from its Greek roots and Islamic heritage to its modern-day significance, makes it a city of multifaceted cultural and historical importance. It’s a testament to the enduring legacy of civilizations and cultures that have contributed to its development over the centuries."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000025",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/m-abnodey-lXAfEKBgAr8-unsplash-2-1.jpg",
